        "<em>porto</em>",
        "<em>portare</em>",
        "<em>-are</em>"
       ],
       [
        "2nd",
        "<em>moneo</em>",
        "<em>monere</em>",
        "<em>-eo</em> and <em>-ere</em>"
       ],
       [
        "3rd",
        "<em>traho</em>",
        "<em>trahere</em>",
        "<em>-o</em> and <em>-ere</em>"
       ],
       [
        "4th",
        "<em>audio</em>",
        "<em>audire</em>",
        "<em>-io</em> and <em>-ire</em>"
       ]
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "note": "The pair to watch is the 2nd and the 3rd: both infinitives end in <em>-ere</em>. The first part decides. <em>video</em> has an <em>e</em> before the <em>-o</em>, so it is 2nd; <em>duco</em> has not, so it is 3rd."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "h2": "Why it matters",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "p": "The conjugation tells you which vowel the verb uses, and so which ending to expect, or to write."
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "servi equos trahunt.",
      "en": "The slaves <b>drag</b> the horses.",
      "note": "<em>traho, trahere</em>: 3rd conjugation, so \"they\" is <em>-unt</em>."
     }
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "viri dominum monent.",
      "en": "The men <b>warn</b> the master.",
      "note": "<em>moneo, monere</em>: 2nd conjugation, so \"they\" is <em>-ent</em>."
     }
    },
    {
     "example": {
      "la": "feminae in villa sedent.",
      "en": "The women <b>sit</b> in the house.",
      "note": "<em>sedeo, sedere</em>: 2nd conjugation, so \"they\" is <em>-ent</em>."
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "watch",
   "h2": "Watch out",
   "exam": true,
   "label": "Common mistakes",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "facts": [
      "An infinitive in <em>-ere</em> could be 2nd or 3rd conjugation. Check the first part: <em>-eo</em> is 2nd.",
      "The first part includes \"I\": <em>moneo</em> is \"I warn\".",
      "The third part is a different tense. <em>monui</em> is \"I warned\": leave it until Chapter 4.",
      "<em>inquit</em>, \"he says\", has no principal parts to learn. It only ever appears in that form, inside a quotation."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
